cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below and also cite the datasets you use."
title: "battery-thermal-management: cooling scheme evaluation and lifetime accounting by simulation"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible PyBaMM-based pipeline that answers two questions for early
  battery thermal management design without a test bench: how much heat a cell
  produces, and how to cool it. Provides an analytic selection map (h x C-rate
  to steady temperature rise), Arrhenius lifetime accounting across cooling
  schemes (4.6x relative lifetime for a cold plate vs natural convection at 3C),
  core-vs-surface temperature diagnostics, and deep-fade failure mechanics
  (band rate acceleration, EIS depth coupling, V(Q) mode split).
version: 1.16.0
date-released: 2026-11-05
license: MIT
